From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 11:57:42 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: kaanapali-oneplus-iceland: the rest of
 stock's USB 2 repeater tuning

Stock's device-mode list for the eUSB2 repeater has five register
overrides, written as <value register> pairs: TUNE_IUSB2 = 14,
TUNE_HSDISC = 7, TUNE_SQUELCH_U = 4, TUNE_USB2_SLEW = 2 and
TUNE_USB2_PREEM = 3. Only the last one was taken over; the amplitude and
the squelch setting stayed at the driver's values for the PM8550B (8 and
3) and the disconnect threshold at the PMIC's default.

Set the amplitude, the disconnect threshold and the squelch setting from
stock's list. The slew rate has no property in the driver yet.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
index b77376fd00a0..601b47203660 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
@@ -1689,7 +1689,13 @@
 	vdd18-supply = <&vreg_l15b_1p8>;
 	vdd3-supply = <&vreg_l5b_3p1>;
 
-	/* stock's device-mode override: TUNE_USB2_PREEM (0x57) = 3 */
+	/*
+	 * stock's device-mode list (qcom,param-override-seq): TUNE_IUSB2 (0x51) = 14, TUNE_HSDISC (0x53) = 7,
+	 * TUNE_SQUELCH_U (0x54) = 4, TUNE_USB2_PREEM (0x57) = 3
+	 */
+	qcom,tune-usb2-amplitude = /bits/ 8 <14>;
+	qcom,tune-usb2-disc-thres = /bits/ 8 <7>;
+	qcom,squelch-detector-bp = <(-2000)>;
 	qcom,tune-usb2-preem = /bits/ 8 <3>;
 };
 
